# [#](#developers) Developers

Developer features allow extending and enhancing Chart.js in many different ways.

## [#](#latest-resources) Latest resources

The latest documentation and samples, including unreleased features, are available at:

- [https://www.chartjs.org/docs/master/  (opens new window)](https://www.chartjs.org/docs/master/)
- [https://www.chartjs.org/samples/master/  (opens new window)](https://www.chartjs.org/samples/master/)

## [#](#development-releases) Development releases

Latest builds are available for testing at:

- [https://www.chartjs.org/dist/master/chart.js  (opens new window)](https://www.chartjs.org/dist/master/chart.js)
- [https://www.chartjs.org/dist/master/chart.umd.min.js  (opens new window)](https://www.chartjs.org/dist/master/chart.umd.min.js)

Warning

Development builds **must not** be used for production purposes or as replacement for a CDN. See [available CDNs](/docs/latest/getting-started/installation.html#cdn).

## [#](#browser-support) Browser support

All modern and up-to-date browsers are supported, including, but not limited to:

- Chrome
- Edge
- Firefox
- Safari

As of version 3, we have dropped Internet Explorer 11 support.

Browser support for the canvas element is available in all modern & major mobile browsers. [CanIUse  (opens new window)](https://caniuse.com/#feat=canvas)

Run `npx browserslist` at the root of the [codebase  (opens new window)](https://github.com/chartjs/Chart.js) to get a list of supported browsers.

Thanks to [BrowserStack  (opens new window)](https://browserstack.com) for allowing our team to test on thousands of browsers.

## [#](#previous-versions) Previous versions

To migrate from version 2 to version 3, please see [the v3 migration guide](../getting-started/v3-migration).

Version 3 has a largely different API than earlier versions.

Most earlier version options have current equivalents or are the same.

Please note - documentation for previous versions is available online or in the GitHub repo.

- [2.9.4 Documentation  (opens new window)](https://www.chartjs.org/docs/2.9.4/)
- [1.x Documentation  (opens new window)](https://github.com/chartjs/Chart.js/tree/v1.1.1/docs)
